			"Message": "style(Mountain): Reflow long lines and brace placement across four files\n\nNormalize formatting in `UpdateValue.rs`, `WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs`, `InitializationData.rs`, and `CocoonService/mod.rs` to align with Rust style conventions. Changes are limited to comment reflow, static declaration compaction, method body compression, and brace positioning — no logic is altered.\n\nCleans up artifacts from prior commits where formatter passes were missed, keeping the codebase consistent.",
			"SHA": "65f1cf26cfa85fc1639f84d0458df61276bfa44a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T05:37:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1574,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add lang-scoped config override, stable session ID\n\n**Language-scoped configuration overrides** — `UpdateValue` now writes into\n`\"[<langId>]\": { key: value }` when the `ConfigurationOverridesDTO` carries a\nnon-empty `OverrideIdentifier`, matching the VS Code convention used by\nprettier-vscode, vscode-eslint, and other per-language formatters. The scope\nkey is cleaned up when its last entry is removed.\n\n**Stable session ID** — `ConstructSandboxConfiguration` and\n`ConstructExtensionHostInitializationData` now share a `OnceLock`-backed\nstatic `SESSION_ID` instead of generating a fresh `Uuid::new_v4()` per call.\nExtensions comparing `telemetryInfo.sessionId` across initialization calls now\nsee a consistent value for the process lifetime.\n\n**Call/Type hierarchy RPC handlers** — `CocoonService` now dispatches\n`$provideCallHierarchyItems`/`prepareCallHierarchy` and\n`$provideTypeHierarchyItems`/`prepareTypeHierarchy` generic requests to\n`Environment::PrepareCallHierarchy` and `PrepareTypeHierarchy` respectively,\nunblocking F12 / Go to References / Call Hierarchy in the editor.\n\n**Real IPC stubs** — `mountain_get_configuration` returns the live merged\nconfig object; `mountain_get_services_status` reports actual Cocoon connection\nstate; `mountain_get_state` surfaces real workspace folder count and active\ndocument URI. Eliminates hardcoded mock data.\n\n**SOCKS proxy support** — Proxy env-var parsing now emits the correct PAC\nkeyword (`SOCKS` for socks/socks4/socks5 URIs, `PROXY` for http/https),\nso extensions using the `proxy` setting work behind SOCKS proxies.\n\n**Dev-log lock contention** — `FlushDedup::Fn` switches from `lock()` to\n`try_lock()` so a contended dedup mutex never parks a Tokio worker thread.\nThe dedup line is cosmetic; missing one flush costs nothing.\n\n**Atomic always-on-top toggle** — Replaces the heuristic title-prefix proxy\nwith a `static AtomicBool` so `nativeHost:toggleWindowAlwaysOnTop` correctly\nflips and sets the opposite state on each invocation.\n\n**ViewColumn forwarding** — The `window.didChangeTextEditorSelection`\nVine notification now includes `viewColumn` from the incoming arguments,\nso extensions calling `activeTextEditor.viewColumn` see the correct pane\nnumber in split-editor layouts.",
			"SHA": "5c627091d0aecbc4b96f536dde7bdf12242cc6f7"
		},
